<h2><span class="emoji">🔁</span>Basic Skills in Football</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Passing:</strong> Moving the ball to a teammate.</li>
  <li><strong>Shooting:</strong> Attempting to score a goal.</li>
  <li><strong>Dribbling:</strong> Controlling the ball while moving.</li>
  <li><strong>Tackling:</strong> Attempting to take the ball from an opponent.</li>
  <li><strong>Positioning:</strong> Being in the right place at the right time.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">📣</span>Key Terms You Should Know</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Offside:</strong> A player is closer to the opponent’s goal line than the ball and second-last defender when the ball is passed to them.</li>
  <li><strong>Penalty Kick:</strong> Awarded for serious fouls inside the penalty area.</li>
  <li><strong>Corner Kick:</strong> Given when the ball crosses the goal line after being last touched by a defender.</li>
  <li><strong>Yellow/Red Card:</strong> Used to discipline players for fouls and misconduct.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">🧠</span>Concept Check</h2>
<ul>
  <li>What happens if the goalkeeper handles the ball outside the penalty area?</li>
  <li>Which team has won the most Premier League titles?</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">💡</span>Summary</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Football is a globally loved sport with simple rules and deep strategy.</li>
  <li>Each team has 11 players with different roles.</li>
  <li>Key competitions include the Premier League and Champions League.</li>
  <li>Skills like passing, dribbling, and shooting are essential.</li>
</ul>

